This perhaps is my best game I ever had in my life. With the
worst possible ending.

Chaotic Elven Ranger, 18 Str, 18 Dex, 16 Con, 16 Int, 20 Wis,
and 11 Cha.

Basic Recap: I went Mines End -> Sokoban -> Mine Town. Found
a =oInvisibility and =oFreeAction. Then turned permanently invisible
thanks to a Stalker. Ranger + invisible is just about the best thing
possible. Found my first spellbook, learned it. Lvl 5 Dig :-/ At 13
base int at this time, I was pretty lucky to learn it. Also found
very early speed boots, which is awesome.

Dropped down and down. Got all important intrinsics that I know of
anyway. Stopped at Medusa's level and went back up for another
sacfest.

When I went back to my stash, I realized that one of my unID'ed
stuff was a /oPoly. I spent about 5000 turns gathering every last
bit of armor on the entire map (killing peaceful elves in the process,
in hopes for elven armor), and another 1000 turns getting every
unicorn horn I could find. Dropped my spare rings in, and zapped.
Gained a saddle, a cloak of protection, oilskin cloak and Hawaiian
shirt.

At the same time, I was going under my normal sac-fest... (had
tons of /oCreateMonster by now) when I made my first mistake.
My first prayer got my crowned :-/ I gained nothing, as I was already
cold and fire resistant, etc. etc. I should have dropped my
luckstone...

So anyway, I went back down to Medusa's level, killed the Titan,
tested my /oCold a bit, and decided to clear my quest instead.

Quest was very easy, especially because no one knew where I
was. Kept missing me :-) Got the LoD, rang the bell (oops, I'll
remember to NOT do that again and save the bell of opening)

Going to the Castle, I had some worries about a polymorph trap. Thanks
RGRN, I like Vampire Lords :-) (though, if anyone knows of a monster
that won't die in 1 hit from a cockatrice because of a bite attack,
please
tell me)

Cleared the Castle, used /oWish to get my first bag of holding
and GDSM. I had 2 reflection sources and cancelation, and so
this pretty much completed my whole kit. I wasn't sure that I was
ready for gehennom yet, so I went back up to search for gold
and get protection.

---------

>From here, I decided to do a sacfest for some reason at max luck.
It was worth it, because 5 spellbooks later, I got my Spellbook of
Identify. 40% fail rate? Who cares! Free ID scrolls. I got healing,
stone-to-flesh and extra healing as well, so I decided to put that
saddle to use.

And hot damn. That was fun. Trained a warhorse to lvl 10 80/80 HP,
and zapped it with a wand of speed. #Ride and I think I'll be forced to
do this again in another game. No more burdened, and I literally am
going some 3x faster than speed boots.

I finished getting my guaranteed protection (down to 0 naked
and -24 with armor), and couldn't find any more enchant armor
scrolls. I decided that with crazy speed (whatever a speedy
warhorse is) and -24 armor  I was sure that I was
ready for gehennom.

And... here is where I messed up. The big YASD.

I stone to flesh a boulder. Cool, huge chunk of meat.

Oh no, killer bee. Kill bee. Eat bee.

You choke.

No warning. o.O Damn, how much nutrition do
those boulders have o.O

